Because of **Soul Shards**. 

In Classic WoW, summoning a Succubus costs a Soul Shard, while summoning a Voidwalker does not. Because the Voidwalker's *Consume Shadows* allows it to regenerate to full health out of combat, it rarely needs to be re-summoned. 

The Succubus, lacking self-healing, dies much more frequently. Constantly spending Soul Shards to re-summon a Succubus after every death or tough fight quickly drains a leveling Warlock's shard bag, making the self-sustaining Voidwalker the more convenient, low-maintenance choice for most players. [end of text]


